# Input for tests/ci/requirements-scons.txt, the hash-locked SCons install used by
# the self-hosted Windows build jobs (baseline_qa.yml, gaussian_production_gates.yml,
# release_builds.yml, release_ci_runtime.yml). Those jobs need nothing else from
# PyPI: no repository script they run imports a third-party module.
#
# Pinned to the SCons the self-hosted runner resolved before the lock existed.
# To upgrade: change the pin here, then run the pip-tools command recorded in
# the header of requirements-scons.txt from the repository root, with
# PIP_CONFIG_FILE set to the null device so a local extra index is never
# consulted. The lock lists the hash of every file PyPI publishes for the pin,
# so it installs on both Windows and Linux.
scons==4.10.1
